{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested: revised MCP head fbf80dea3ec8994dc9ee3deb0bda664d8446b2ee, tree 2f45b59437010e42fec8d384def30ba5330ddd1e. The thirteen earlier repair clusters are substantially addressed, but the following functional and boundary cases remain.\n\nP1 — Complete native no-act capability preparation (service.ts425–427; room story113–122).\nGeneric prepare requires target/kind and builds a declared act. It cannot send hold@1:instance, so an accepted native hold instance→stage/check→hand-in workflow remains unreachable. The revised real-Worker story accurately proves not-staged refusals, not successful preparation. Add the native standalone capability-step operation under exact custody and prove that complete workflow with preparation and act lifecycles separate. The note acknowledges this omission; it is not completion of W1–W7.\n\nP2 — Complete the successful full proposal witness (recipes.scope.test.ts201–219).\nThe new recipe uses one file, then expects propose-manifest to refuse source-shape. It proves that refusal, not artroom propose acceptance/merge, and n=1 cannot witness multi-file selection. Use the applicable change3/destination3 cohort with at least two files, actual trees, accepted version and merge, and update the counts from the executed successful recipe. Keep the current refusal evidence at its own subject.\n\nP2 — Capacity admission must include refused resubmissions (custody.ts237–276).\n#kept returns an existing refusal before the shared capacity lease. send then increments its attempt and writes sent outside that lease. With256 unresolved records, resubmitting another retained refusal creates257; concurrent resubmissions do the same. Re-admit terminal→unresolved transitions and persist them within the shared lease before delivery. Failed admission must preserve the prior refusal. Extend the two-process test beyond new identities.\n\nP2 — Recover a decisive outcome when all inline outcomes spilled (custody.ts195–218).\n#outcome can spill every outcome to meet the2MiB record bound. decided then sees outcomes[0]?.attempt as undefined, returns null and never reads the nonempty segment. A retained accepted/mismatch send becomes unreadable despite its outcome being kept. Add the empty-inline segment fallback and prove send/settle recover it without a new signature or delivery.\n\nP2 — Make lease reclamation and release ownership-safe (node.ts59–94).\nTwo reclaimers can both read a dead owner; A replaces it with a live lease, then B unconditionally unlinks A's replacement and acquires too. Unconditional release can remove a newer owner's lease. Identity, capacity and archive exclusions all depend on this primitive. Use serialized recovery/ownership and owner-specific release; a separate reread alone still races. Witness simultaneous reclaimers with only one entry to the protected work.\n\nP2 — Recheck archival eligibility after taking the record lock (node.ts114–123).\nCandidates are selected as terminal before locking; current bytes are then moved without rechecking phase. A refusal resubmitted to unknown between selection and lock is archived and removed from the live-only unresolved count. Revalidate phase/eligibility under the lock, preserving unresolved enumeration/admission, and witness this interleaving.\n\nP2 — Refresh an externally added root even when its tool name is known (service.ts172/231–232).\nOwn configuration writes now invalidate correctly. A second process adding a second garden root does not: #current remains cached and refreshes only for an unknown tool name. The added test creates the first garden.plant name, exercising that old fallback. For a known name at a new root under a second membership, the stale mapping can choose the repository membership, changing member shaping/custody binding. Detect the needed configuration revision or refresh on calls, and witness that case without a list/room preflight.\n\nP2 — Bound the entire settlement/preparation result (service.ts93–97/649–655).\nok removes duplicated text but leaves oversized structuredContent unchanged. settle returns all retained steps and their full latest native Answers with no cursor; many legitimate foreign-resource steps can exceed4KiB while fitting the custody record. Preparation likewise returns the full native Answer. Page/reference the complete step/answer projection under the whole-response limit, preserving every receipt and step. The large-live-item exception does not cover arbitrary custody results.\n\nP2 — Make multi-membership role text deterministic and truthful (catalogue.ts184–192/244–257).\nwhoOf renders known[0].role for all-hold/all-lack, in inventory encounter order. Reordering two memberships with different roles changes the description while sorted generation inputs remain identical. Render a deterministic aggregate/per-membership account and test two different roles; the new single-membership reorder test misses it. Native authorization is unaffected.\n\nP2 — Close subscriptions that disconnect before initial snapshot resolves (wire.ts202; node.ts377).\ndropStream removes the map and initial noop unsubscribe while snapshot is pending. The continuation still installs a watcher after closure, now absent from cleanup maps. Mark ended and check ownership/attachment around installation; unsubscribe immediately if closure wins. A deferred-snapshot, pre-ack disconnect witness must leave no watcher/listen/timer.\n\nP2 — Validate request IDs/methods and bound reflected wire errors (wire.ts65/112/162).\nisFrame checks object/jsonrpc only. IDs of object/array/boolean shape can be echoed; malformed request methods disappear as though they were valid response frames. Unsupported version is reflected twice and unknown method verbatim, allowing multi-megabyte errors within the4MiB input allowance. Distinguish valid request/notification/response frames, reject invalid IDs with null, and cap reflected diagnostics. Witness large IDs/version/method and containment. No signer bypass or stored-secret leak is claimed.\n\nP2 — Narrow/document the invitation non-echo guarantee without falsifying history (service.ts740/761/555–565).\nThe successful admitted join retains the exact signed input containing fields.secret. Generic step/record returns those native bytes, whole or in complete slices. Direct join result is safe; “no result repeats the invitation secret” in the note/descriptor is false. Preserve native record/hash fidelity: qualify the guarantee to direct join and document authorized history's secret-bearing bytes, or define an explicit restricted/redacted representation with integrity limits. Do not silently mask an exact record.\n\nReceiving-main composition remains required.\nAgainst current receiving6198b199, this candidate has110 differences,52 outside its58 bound artifacts, including the landed documentation, Home copy/layout and observability note. This is a native comparison, not a claim that normal three-way merge necessarily overwrites them. Deliver an exact composed head demonstrating their preservation before landing.\n\nP3 cleanup: items prose/fixture promises live then retained traversal, but final:true is a separate traversal. State both. wire.ts's opening SDK rationale is the false premise already withdrawn in the note; correct it while retaining the separately justified minimal handler.\n\nArchitecture/Security/Simplification: credited repairs include MCP-only join with key reuse/exact lost-request/readback, newest decisive current-attempt truth, explicit separate step retention, shared new-record admission, byte-aware spilling, own-write refresh, escaped text/room byte paging, resumable searches, named-rule/profile/mark digests, partly unknown standing, presented-fact schemas, capability exceptions, fatal one-decode UTF8, request containment, per-stream listens and bounded/pruned stdio. Revised per-call/per-page/70-retry/cold-warm budget witnesses fix prior measurement defects. Keep them and the full functionality. Hosted stage2, optional CLI guide and credential3reads are explicitly owed in original dd024; they are not falsely declared complete here.\n\nCoverage/validation: reporting note FIRST FULL Root19932B304LF SHA821d4c3263c1dc1cbc7d9a06ebb587073a9866fdc30348fcb61c5d88301f6774. All58 bound artifacts covered by fresh/logical FULL peers and exact prior inheritance; five final reports and bounded audits FULL Root. Native body/delta/line reconstructions independently verified. JSON fixture243961B SHA3a2c3ce6… has FULL lossless data-token coverage145949B SHA187beeba…, preserving key order, duplicate keys, strings/escapes/numbers; NOT raw BODY FULL. Its12922 raw runs/98012 removed outside-string whitespace bytes are independently reconstructed. Lock retains prior adopted-entry coverage with whole native equality; indices retain row-only coverage. Root whole modules remain PARTIAL, with complete selected findings units read. Audit /Users/hughpyle/play/artroom-checker-state/mcp-fbf-root/native-audit.json4950B SHA693ad922449bcaddd647684716279ab5bff0d94d3cce6bdd537e1c6aab2cf528; composition-audit.json1714B SHAef09e0ff58967d98e7e0c00ac76d1fc6c9ba1f380332d1dd42e4a0590182c1c8.\n\nOwner reports cloud4-checker failures and exact local fbf gate1099 pass/2skips/0fail, with the Node26 child-warning amendment. No explicitly CLOSED local gate projection has arrived; raw logs/scratchpad/programs are unread, and no independent runtime/whole-green claim is made. Checker ran no Source/tests/gate/build/install/provider/browser/recipes or new cloud session. Normal prepare assigns dd024/7012/main, primary first/all58, no override. This head is not approved or complete.\n","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:c2873ee6bc4a46c882ab8fd112e77ad16d603679","binding":"assigned","head":"fbf80dea3ec8994dc9ee3deb0bda664d8446b2ee","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:f9f162c11cd09858996f437cb040634df0926241